# HC-043 reference notes

SYNTHETIC_TRAINING_ONLY

Checked against public GitHub documentation on 2026-09-15. This is a short training summary, not a product schema or live account observation.

## Boundaries to preserve

- Cloud Agents Automations may be triggered by schedules or repository events, but product eligibility, repository visibility, and policy must be checked separately.
- Creator, event actor, billing subject, repository reader, session viewer, and stop/resume owner may differ.
- A private automation configuration does not imply that the resulting session has the same visibility.
- A read-only analysis task does not need label, review, commit, push, or other write effects.
- Duplicate events and synchronized PR heads require an identity and staleness policy; the training fields do not claim a built-in dedup setting.
- Cloud Agents Automations, standard code review rulesets, and Copilot App scheduled workflows have overlapping UI concepts without becoming one storage/API/runtime contract.

## Public references

- https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/agents/cloud-agent/about-automations
- https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/copilot-on-github/set-up-copilot/configure-code-review

Automation creation, event firing, session execution, tool use, billing, stop, and resume are `not-observed`.
